VAL_ 128 FAULT_Node 1 "Pedalbox" 2 "Dashboard" 3 "Rear" 4 "TTCS" 5 "Charger" ;
VAL_ 578 ECU_DashMode 1 "Accel" 2 "Skidpad" 3 "AutoX" 4 "Endurance" 5 "Custom" ;
VAL_ 578 ECU_StartStage 0 "NotAvailable" 1 "Wait" 2 "PressBrake" 3 "PressStart" 4 "ReadyToDrive" ;

CM_ BO_ 1760 "MUR ADDITION (PROVISIONAL, bench/demo): parameter-storage request endpoint for node 0, ID 0x6E0 + node. Classic-CAN ISO-TP: this frame is one 8-byte fragment (ISO-TP PCI byte + 7 data bytes), reassembled by the parameter service; telemetry must not treat the bytes as signals. Reserved block 0x6E0-0x6E7 requests, 0x6E8-0x6EF responses; canboot uses 0x7E0/0x7E8. ISO-TP flow control for a request arrives on 0x6E8 + node. Wire format, catalog and validation: generated/params/mur_params.h and mur_msgs.params. No parameter signal is finalized and no proto exists.";
CM_ BO_ 1768 "MUR ADDITION (PROVISIONAL, bench/demo): parameter-storage response endpoint for node 0, ID 0x6E8 + node. ISO-TP fragment of the shared 16-byte header plus at most 4096 payload bytes; see PARAM_Request and generated/params/mur_params.h. Never decoded as a signal.";
BA_ "GenMsgSendType" BO_ 1760 2;
BA_ "GenMsgSendType" BO_ 1768 2;
